Those are really smart questions, Alex. Let me give you the honest rundown on Can Paixano.

On the crowding - yes, it's genuinely chaotic, especially during peak hours between 7 and 9 PM when locals pile in after work. But here's the thing: that chaos is actually part of what makes it authentic. There's an energy to it, everyone's shoulder to shoulder, glasses clinking, hams hanging from the ceiling. If you go a bit earlier, say around 6 PM, or later around 9:30, it's more manageable but still has that buzz. You'll need to be a little assertive getting to the bar, but it's friendly chaos, not aggressive.

