**MY RECOMMENDATION: Can Paixano (La Xampanyeria)**

**Why it's worth going:**
This is a standing-room-only cava bar in Barceloneta that's been serving locals since 1969. There are no tables, no seats, no English menus, no Instagram moments. You elbow your way to the bar, shout your order in Spanish if you can manage it, and they keep a mental tab until you leave. It's chaotic, loud, wine-stained, and completely unpretentious. This is where locals go after work to drink €1.50 glasses of house cava and eat enormous bocadillos. It has a 4.3 rating, very high local popularity, and moderate tourist awareness — meaning you'll be one of the few visitors who found it.

**What to order:**
- **House pink cava** (rosado) — their signature, absurdly cheap, surprisingly good
