- Bocadillo mixto (ham + cheese)
- Just point at the cured meats hanging from the ceiling — they'll carve to order

Don't even think about menú del día — this is about standing at the bar, drinking cava, and eating cured pork.

**The vibe:** Standing room only, wine-stained barrels, hams hanging from the ceiling, locals shouting orders in Catalan, you will be elbow-to-elbow with strangers. Dress code: whatever you're wearing. Noise level: very loud.

**Price:** €10-15 per person total. I'm serious. A few glasses of cava and a massive bocadillo.

**Getting a spot:** No reservations (there are no tables). Just show up. Peak chaos is 7-9pm (after-work crowd). Go at 6pm or after 9:30pm for slightly less madness.

**Signs it's genuinely local:**
- Menu is handwritten in Spanish only, on a chalkboard
- Staff speaks Spanish/Catalan — English is an afterthought
- Cash only
- Closed Sundays (locals rest)
- 80%+ local crowd
- No website, no Instagram presence, no online reservations
- You will feel slightly lost — that's correct

