Picture this: you elbow your way to a bar surrounded by locals, hams hanging from the ceiling, wine stains on everything, and you order glasses of their house pink cava for about €1.50 each. Yes, €1.50. You pair it with enormous bocadillos stuffed with jamón ibérico carved right there, manchego, fuet—simple, perfect Catalan bar food.

