It is lovely to hear from you again, Alex! I am so glad our previous consultation served you well. Paris is a city close to my heart, and finding the right spot there can truly define your trip.

Since you are looking to dive into the scene, I have a recommendation that offers arguably the most iconic atmosphere in the city. It is called **Café de la Tour**. 

Located right in the 7th Arrondissement, this brasserie offers a stunning, direct view of the Eiffel Tower from its terrace—it is quite the spectacle, especially during the light show. They serve all the classic staples you would expect, like Coq au vin and French onion soup, in a very elegant, English-friendly setting. It creates that picture-perfect Parisian moment that many travelers dream of. 

How does a dinner with a panoramic view of the Iron Lady sound to start your Parisian adventure?

